DevOps Internship - Week 2 Report

-> Introduction
During Week 2 I learned Git and GitHub by creating repositories, committing files and working with
branches.

-> Git
Git is a distributed version control system that tracks changes and maintains project history.

-> GitHub
GitHub hosts Git repositories online and enables collaboration.

-> Git Workflow
I created a repository, cloned it, added files, committed changes and pushed them to GitHub.

-> Branching and Merge
I created feature branches and merged them into the main branch after completing my work.

-> Rebase
Rebase creates a cleaner commit history by replaying commits onto another branch.

-> Pull Requests
Pull Requests are used for reviewing and merging changes.

-> README.md
README.md explains the project and provides useful information.

-> .gitignore
.gitignore excludes unnecessary files from version control.

-> Conclusion
This week's tasks improved my understanding of version control and collaboration using Git and
GitHub.
